't exist yet. I need to:\n\n1. First ask the user for clarification, or\n2. Create page 2 first, then figure out how to move widgets\n\nBut I don't have a \"move widget\" tool. Looking at the available tools, I can:\n- delete_widget: Remove a widget from a page\n- create_widget: Place a widget on a page\n- There's no direct \"move widget\" function\n\nAlso, there's no way to just get widget info without a specific tool. Let me check if there's a way to get widget information from the page.\n\nActually, I should inform the user about the current situation:\n1. Only page 1 exists, page 2 doesn't exist\n2. There's no direct \"move\" function - I would need to recreate widgets on the new page and delete from the old one\n\nLet me also note that for setting a background, the create_page function has a \"background\" parameter, but it only accepts a color value, not an image path. I should clarify this with the user.\n\nLet me ask the user for more information about:\n1. What widgets are on page 1 (or I can try to get them)\n2. The background image they want (though the system might only support colors)\n\nActually, let me try to get widget info first. But I don't see a \"list_widgets\" function. The get_widget function exists but I don't know what parameters it needs.\n\nLet me inform the user about the situation and ask for clarification."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 128586, "output_tokens": 634, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 22376.10609998228}, "judge": null}
