 "input_tokens": 64221, "output_tokens": 633, "latency_ms": 15429.983099980745, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "好的！我来帮你搭建一个完整的泵站控制台，包含点位定义、HMI界面、启停控制和报警配置。先创建基础点位：", "reasoning": "The user wants to create a pump station control console with start/stop controls, and also set up alarms. Let me break this down:\n\n1. Create SCADA points for the pump (status, control, maybe speed/current)\n2. Create HMI pages with pump widgets and controls\n3. Set up alarms for the pump\n4. Bind points to widgets\n\nLet me start by creating the necessary points and then work on the HMI layout and alarms.\n\nI'll create:\n- PUMP_01_STATUS (digital - running/stopped)\n- PUMP_01_CMD (digital - start/stop command)\n- PUMP_01_SPEED (analog - speed feedback)\n- PUMP_01_CURRENT (analog - motor current)\n- PUMP_01_VIBRATION (analog - vibration for alarm)\n\nThen create a page, add widgets, bind points, and create alarms.\n\nLet me start with creating the points first, as they're foundational. I can create multiple independent points at once."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 65043, "output_tokens": 107, "latency_ms": 2507.0388999884017, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "点位创建完成！现在创建 HMI 控制台页面和控件：", "reasoning": "Points created successfully. Now let me create the HMI page and add widgets for the pump station control console."}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 65187, "output_tokens": 794, "latency_ms": 16990.90990005061, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "页面创建成功！添加泵体和仪表控件：", "reasoning": "Good, page created. Now let me add widgets - pump, thermometer-like displays, buttons, etc."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 66179, "output_tokens": 665, "latency_ms": 9646.865300019272, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "添加文字标签和点位绑定：", "reasoning": "Good, widgets created. Now add text labels and bind points to widgets."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 67160, "output_tokens": 671, "latency_ms": 14528.325099963695, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "绑定点位到控件，并创建报警：", "reasoning": "Good, now let me bind the points to widgets and create the alarms."}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 68194, "output_tokens": 252, "latency_ms": 4392.6255000405945, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "报警参数需要调整，重新创建模拟量报警：", "reasoning": "The analog alarms had issues with null values. Let me retry without the null parameters - just don't pass them."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 68576, "output_tokens": 276, "latency_ms": 4640.271999989636, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "尝试提供双限值：", "reasoning": "It seems the schema has an issue with optional parameters. Let me try providing both limits explicitly."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 68982, "output_tokens": 272, "latency_ms": 8372.750099981204, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "Something is wrong with the schema parsing. Let me try with explicit numbers only (no strings) and see what happens. Actually looking at the error, it says \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - but I'm providing numbers. Let me try using just the required fields first.\n\nActually wait, looking at the function definition again:\n```\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}\n```\n\nThe schema says it can be number or null. But I'm providing -1 which is a number. The error message says \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" which suggests somewhere it's being parsed as a string.\n\nLet me try a simpler call with just required params to see if it works."}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 69300, "output_tokens": 85, "latency_ms": 4482.237799966242, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "This is strange. Let me try passing the parameters without the action parameter, or maybe there's a formatting issue. Let me try a very minimal call."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 69433, "output_tokens": 119, "latency_ms": 4285.503899969626, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "This is really odd - it's complaining about low_limit even when I don't provide it. The default is null but it seems like the backend is trying to parse null as a number. This might be a backend bug. Let me try providing both limits explicitly as floats."}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 69600, "output_tokens": 335, "latency_ms": 10260.046399955172, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "This is clearly a bug in the system. Let me check if there's something else going on. Maybe the issue is with how I'm formatting the JSON. Let me try a different approach - maybe I should use the set_threshold or another method to work around this.\n\nActually, let me re-read the function signature more carefully. The schema says:\n```\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}\n```\n\nBut I wonder if there's a strict mode issue. The \"strict\" parameter is set to false. Let me try without the action parameter since it has a default.\n\nActually wait, I notice the error says \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - this error keeps appearing even when I pass 0 or -1. It seems like maybe the system is expecting a specific format. Let me try passing it as a string number format.\n\nActually, the error message is confusing because I AM passing a number. This could be a backend issue. Let me try once more with explicit formatting. If it still fails, I'll proceed with what we have and note the limitation.\n\nLet me try passing the number differently."}, {"turn": 12, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 69983, "output_tokens": 151, "latency_ms": 5602.651999972295, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "This is very strange. The parameter is being sent as a number but the system is complaining about parsing a string. There may be a bug in the function or the backend. Let me try one more time with just the required parameters and see what happens. If it still fails, I'll proceed and inform the user about this limitation.\n\nActually, let me try without specifying low_limit at all - just required and high_limit."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 811858, "output_tokens": 4360, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 103619.7132000234}, "judge": null}
