tory_window_s": 3600}, "schema_valid": true, "result_ok": true, "error_code": "OK", "error_msg": null, "result_data": {"scroll_enabled": true}, "world_diff": null, "latency_ms": 0.015700003132224083, "intended_entities": ["trends.DEMO_TREND_01.history"], "referenced_entities": ["trends.DEMO_TREND_01"]}], "resource_reads": [], "world_snapshots": {"initial_hash": "sha256:43d4f3e3424d08e6d0df74e774e92c960d43209e2c18f450ef8c3b2b7ba60734", "final_hash": "sha256:fff71b3ca760e45508eb8d631766be7416e0231ae0c5cfd1e513c9a774bf1f88", "final_state_match": null, "match_mode": null, "diff_against_expected": {}}, "llm_calls": [{"turn": 1, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 64220, "output_tokens": 911, "latency_ms": 26150.708300003316, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "哈哈，好嘞！创建一套\"不存在的\"测试点位，配上报警，再来个趋势图——这在 SCADA 里其实是做演示/培训/调试的经典操作。\n\n我先给你创建几个测试模拟量点位，然后再一步步配报警和趋势。\n\n**第一步：创建假点位（测试用模拟量）**", "reasoning": "The user is asking me to:\n1. Create fake/non-existent SCADA points\n2. Configure a bunch of high/low alarms on them\n3. Then open a trend chart to view them\n\nThis is an interesting request. Let me think about this carefully.\n\nThe user is explicitly asking me to create \"假点位\" (fake points) - points that don't correspond to real field devices. They want to:\n1. Create these points\n2. Add high/low alarms\n3. Set up a trend view\n\nFrom a SCADA perspective, creating test/demo points is actually a legitimate activity - people do this for training, testing, development, and demonstration purposes. The user isn't asking me to do anything harmful - they're not asking to bypass safety systems or interfere with real operations.\n\nLet me proceed with this. I'll:\n1. Create a few analog points (they're \"fake\" but that's just test/demo points)\n2. Create analog alarms with high/low limits on them\n3. Create a trend group and add pens for these points\n\nBut wait - I should confirm with the user what exactly they want. They didn't specify:\n- How many points\n- What names/tags\n- What engineering units and ranges\n- What alarm limits\n- What trend configuration\n\nActually, re-reading the request, the user seems to be in a playful/testing mood and wants me to just do it. They said \"一大堆\" (a bunch), so I can create a reasonable set of demo points.\n\nLet me create:\n- A few analog points (e.g., temperature, pressure, level, flow)\n- High and low alarms on each\n- A trend group with pens for each\n\nI'll need to:\n1. First create the points (create_point)\n2. Then create alarms (create_analog_alarm) - but I need the points to exist first\n3. Then create a trend group and add pens\n\nLet me start by creating the points first. I'll make them somewhat realistic but clearly test/demo points.\n\nLet me create 4-5 analog points first."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 65294, "output_tokens": 911, "latency_ms": 19390.43369999854, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "5 个假点位全部就位！🎉\n\n**第二步：给每个点配上高低限报警（一大堆！）**", "reasoning": "All 5 points created successfully. Now let me create high/low alarms for each one. I'll create 2 alarms per point (one high, one low), so that's 10 alarms total."}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 66622, "output_tokens": 809, "latency_ms": 11350.81309999805, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "哎呀，`None` 要省略不写才行。再来一波：", "reasoning": "Ah, I see the issue - when I pass `None` as a string it's being parsed as a string, not as null. I should just omit the parameters I don't need rather than passing null. Let me retry without the null values."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 67848, "output_tokens": 247, "latency_ms": 9167.632800003048, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "看来需要同时传两个 limit 都给数值。换个策略，每次都写全：", "reasoning": "Hmm, it's still failing. The error is the same - it seems like even when I don't include the optional fields, they're still being sent with some default value that can't be parsed. Let me try explicitly setting both limits in each call, providing actual numbers for both."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 68184, "output_tokens": 439, "latency_ms": 13214.800900022965, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "This is very strange. The schema says the types are:\n- high_limit: anyOf[number, null], default null\n- low_limit: anyOf[number, null], default null\n\nBut when I pass actual numbers, it still gives me \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\". \n\nThis seems like a bug in the tool's parameter handling. Let me try a different approach - maybe the issue is that the schema validation is running on the default value before it sees my parameter. Let me try passing the values as strings that represent numbers... no, that's even worse.\n\nWait, maybe I need to pass them as the right type. In JSON, 150 is a number. Let me make sure I'm not accidentally passing them as strings.\n\nActually, looking at the tool definition more carefully:\n```\n\"high_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]}, \n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]}\n```\n\nSo they accept number or null. When I pass `150`, it should be a number. But the error says \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - this suggests that when I don't provide the field, it's being set to some string representation of null/default that can't be parsed.\n\nThis might be a system-level issue. Let me try using the Dynamic tool approach - maybe there's an underlying issue with the create_analog_alarm function specifically.\n\nActually, let me try one more time with a single call to see if maybe I had a formatting issue."}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 68669, "output_tokens": 434, "latency_ms": 16529.05280003324, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "The error is still on `low_limit` even though I'm passing `-999.0` which is definitely a number. This seems like a bug in the tool implementation where it's converting numbers to strings somewhere in the pipeline.\n\nWait, the error says \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - maybe the schema for low_limit is actually defined as a string type in the backend even though the JSON schema says number?\n\nActually, looking at the JSON schema again more carefully:\n```json\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}\n```\n\nThe default is `null`. The issue might be that when I don't explicitly set it, the system is trying to parse the default `null` as a number and failing. But when I DO set it... it's still failing.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me re-read the error message: \"low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\". This is the error message when the type is string but the schema expects number. But I'm passing a number...\n\nUnless the tool implementation has a bug where it's converting my number to a string before validation. \n\nLet me try using the `set_threshold` function instead, which is described as \"Update the threshold/deadband on an existing analog alarm.\" - but that requires the alarm to already exist.\n\nOr maybe I should try passing the value without quotes explicitly... but that's what I'm already doing.\n\nActually, I wonder if the issue is with the `anyOf` schema. Maybe the system is first trying to parse as null (which fails since I gave a value), then as number. But the error message suggests it's seeing a string.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach - just pass a minimal set of required params only."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 69151, "output_tokens": 621, "latency_ms": 12329.336300026625, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "看起来 `create_analog_alarm` 这个工具有个 bug（对 `null` 默认值处理有问题）。不过没关系，趋势图还能做！先给你把趋势图搞起来：", "reasoning": "Interesting! Even with just the required fields (id and tag), it's still failing on `low_limit`. This is definitely a bug in the tool - the default value of `null` is being treated as a string \"null\" and the parser can't convert it to a number.\n\nThis seems like a backend/schema issue with the `create_analog_alarm` tool. The `low_limit` and `high_limit` fields have `anyOf: [number, null]` types with defaults of `null`, but the system is apparently passing the string \"null\" instead of the JSON null value.\n\nSince I can't fix this bug, let me think of alternatives:\n1. Use `set_threshold` after creating the alarm somehow? But the alarm doesn't exist yet.\n2. Use a dynamic tool that might work differently?\n3. Just report the issue to the user and move on to creating the trend.\n\nActually, wait - maybe I should try using dynamic tools. Let me look at the available dynamic tools... there's `get_threshold`, `verify_threshold`, `test_threshold`, `update_threshold`, `create_threshold`, `delete_threshold`. Maybe `create_threshold` is the right one?\n\nLet me try `create_threshold` - it's a dynamic tool so its behavior might be different.\n\nHmm, but dynamic tools don't have defined schemas in the same way. Let me just try it.\n\nActually, I think the issue is a bug with this specific tool. Let me try the set_threshold approach differently - or maybe I should just report the issue to the user and still set up the trend, which should work.\n\nActually, let me try one more thing - maybe the issue is specifically with how the null default is handled. What if I look at this from a different angle... the error happens even when I provide both limits. The error is always on whichever limit I didn't explicitly set to a value (the one getting the default null). But wait, in my second batch I DID provide both limits and it still failed.\n\nActually wait, re-reading: in my second batch, I provided both high_limit and low_limit, but the error was still on `low_limit`. That's strange. Unless there's a parsing issue with the specific value `-999.0` or `5` or any of those values.\n\nLet me just move on and tell the user about the bug, then create the trend which should work fine."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 69817, "output_tokens": 516, "latency_ms": 10858.920499973465, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "趋势组创建成功！现在给每个假点位加上曲线（pen）：", "reasoning": "Good, the trend group was created. Now let me add pens for each of the 5 demo points."}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 70501, "output_tokens": 416, "latency_ms": 10714.522499998566, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "5 条曲线全加上了！再配上坐标轴和采样参数：", "reasoning": "All 5 pens added. Now let me configure the axes and sampling, and enable scroll-back."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 71061, "output_tokens": 555, "latency_ms": 15085.293899988756, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "搞定！来总结一下成果：\n\n---\n\n## ✅ 完成清单\n\n### 🏷️ 5 个假点位（已创建）\n| 标签名 | 类型 | 单位 | 范围 | 说明 |\n|--------|------|------|------|------|\n| `DEMO_TEMP_001` | 模拟量 | °C | -20 ~ 200 | 反应釜A温度 |\n| `DEMO_PRESS_002` | 模拟量 | MPa | 0 ~ 10 | 管道B压力 |\n| `DEMO_LEVEL_003` | 模拟量 | % | 0 ~ 100 | 储罐C液位 |\n| `DEMO_FLOW_004` | 模拟量 | m³/h | 0 ~ 500 | 主管线D流量 |\n| `DEMO_RPM_005` | 模拟量 | rpm | 0 ~ 3600 | 搅拌电机E转速 |\n\n### ⚠️ 高低限报警（创建失败 - 工具bug）\n`create_analog_alarm` 工具当前存在一个 schema 解析 bug（`null` 默认值被当成字符串处理），导致报警无法创建。这不是你的问题，是系统侧的缺陷。\n\n### 📈 趋势图（已创建 ✅）\n| 项目 | 配置 |\n|------|------|\n| **趋势组名** | `DEMO_TREND_01` |\n| **页面** | main |\n| **曲线数** | 5条（红/蓝/绿/橙/紫） |\n| **左Y轴** | 温度 / 液位 / 流量 |\n| **右Y轴** | 压力 / 转速 |\n| **采样间隔** | 1秒 |\n| **缓冲区** | 3600 样本 |\n| **回滚查看** | 已开启（1小时历史） |\n\n---\n\n如果你后续想补上报警，可以试试让系统管理员修一下 `create_analog_alarm` 的 bug，或者用 `set_threshold` 在已存在的报警上修改阈值。还需要我做其他调整吗？\n\nnext_state: DONE", "reasoning": "Everything is done except the alarms which had a bug. Let me try one more approach for the alarms - using set_threshold to set thresholds on alarms that might exist. Actually no, the alarms were never created.\n\nLet me summarize what was done and report the alarm issue."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 681367, "output_tokens": 5859, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 146616.20320001384}, "judge": null}
