vention uses \"R12\" prefix, not \"REACTOR_12\". Let me check if there are more points by looking at the template page's bindings or create the remaining points with the R12_ prefix convention.\n\nLet me create the temperature and alarm points with R12_ prefix and then bind them."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 67777, "output_tokens": 393, "latency_ms": 8741.122600040399, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "点位创建完成！现在绑定罐体和组件的数据：", "reasoning": "All points created successfully. Now let me bind them to the widgets."}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 68347, "output_tokens": 87, "latency_ms": 3840.496299962979, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我验证一下点位是否已正确创建：", "reasoning": "Hmm, it seems like there's some caching or the previous tag names are being used. Let me verify the points exist first and try again. It might be a timing issue or the system might be using different point names. Let me list points again to confirm."}, {"turn": 12, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 68507, "output_tokens": 311, "latency_ms": 7313.044600014109, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "看起来点位可能存在同步问题，让我重新创建并立即绑定：", "reasoning": "Interesting - it seems the points I just created (R12_TEMP, R12_PRESSURE, R12_ALARM) are not showing up in the list, only the original R12_LEVEL. But the create_point calls returned success. This might be a simulation/test environment issue.\n\nLet me try creating the points again and then binding."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 793972, "output_tokens": 3574, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 96480.34710000502}, "judge": null}
