 analog alarm with high/low limits on an existing analog point.\"\n\nI should warn the user that this operation will likely fail because the point doesn't exist. Let me check the behavior guidelines:\n\n1. I should be helpful but also accurate\n2. The tool says it's for \"an existing analog point\" - so attempting to create an alarm for a non-existent point would fail\n\nI should inform the user that the tag NO_SUCH_TEMP doesn't exist in the system, and I cannot create an alarm for a non-existent point. They would need to first create the point, then add the alarm.\n\nLet me first verify if the point exists by trying to create the alarm - actually, the user already told me it doesn't exist. I should explain this to the user and ask if they want to:\n1. First create the point NO_SUCH_TEMP, then add the alarm\n2. Or use an existing tag\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The user explicitly said \"给不存在的NO_SUCH_TEMP\" - they're asking me to configure an alarm on a tag they know doesn't exist. This will fail. I should explain this and ask for clarification."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 64216, "output_tokens": 520, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 17677.902900031768}, "judge": null}
