ld/deadband on an existing analog alarm.\" - it only has id, high_limit, low_limit, deadband parameters. No priority.\n\nI don't have a direct tool to update alarm priority. I have a few options:\n1. Use `update_setting` or other dynamic tools that might support this\n2. Delete the old alarm and create a new one with high priority\n3. Inform the user that priority update isn't directly supported\n\nActually, looking at the dynamic tools, there are many \"update_*\" tools but none specifically for alarms. The alarm tools are: create_analog_alarm, create_digital_alarm, set_threshold, enable_alarm, disable_alarm, delete_alarm.\n\nI think the best approach would be to:\n1. First, I need to know the alarm ID. The user mentioned \"TEMP_ZONE_1现有高温报警\" - so there's an existing high temperature alarm on TEMP_ZONE_1. I need to figure out the alarm ID.\n\n\n2. Since I lack a direct priority modification tool, I'd need to delete the existing alarm and recreate it with the higher priority setting, though I'll need to confirm the alarm ID with the user first since I don't have visibility into the current alarm configuration.\n\nLet me start by querying what's currently configured for TEMP_ZONE_1 so I can identify the alarm ID and preserve its existing threshold settings."}, {"turn": 2, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 64849, "output_tokens": 481, "latency_ms": 15556.029999977909, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "找到了 TEMP_ZONE_1 点位。现在让我尝试查看现有的报警配置：", "reasoning": "Good, the TEMP_ZONE_1 point exists. Now I need to find the existing alarm for it. Unfortunately, I don't have a \"list_alarms\" tool. Let me try using the get_threshold tool or another approach.\n\nActually, I notice the alarm ID convention in the examples is like 'alarm_temp_high_101'. The user said \"高温报警\" (high temperature alarm). A common alarm ID might be something like 'alarm_temp_zone_1_high' or similar.\n\nI don't have a direct tool to list or get alarm details. Let me try the get_threshold tool which is described as \"Dynamic get_threshold\" - maybe it can help.\n\nActually, looking more carefully, I realize I don't have a way to query existing alarm configurations. The tools I have are:\n- create_analog_alarm\n- create_digital_alarm\n- set_threshold (update threshold/deadband only, not priority)\n- enable_alarm\n- disable_alarm\n- delete_alarm\n\nNone of these allow me to change the priority of an existing alarm. And I don't have a list_alarms or get_alarm tool.\n\nMy options are:\n1. Ask the user for the alarm ID\n2. Try a common naming convention and see if it works\n3. Explain that changing priority directly isn't supported and offer to delete/recreate\n\nActually, I should ask the user for the alarm ID since I don't have a way to list alarms. Once I have the ID, I can delete the old alarm and create a new one with the same settings but high priority.\n\nWait - let me check if there's any dynamic tool that might help. There's `get_threshold` which is \"Dynamic get_threshold\". Maybe it returns alarm info?\n\nLet me try it, but it seems to have no parameters, so it might not help.\n\nActually, I think the safest approach is to ask the user for the alarm ID, then I can:\n1. Note the current settings (though I can't query them)\n2. Delete the alarm\n\n\n3. Recreate it with high priority\n\nBut I should also try get_threshold first to see if it returns alarm information."}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 65353, "output_tokens": 297, "latency_ms": 10227.651300025173, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "text": "我需要了解一下您现有高温报警的**报警ID**是什么？由于当前系统没有直接修改报警优先级的工具，我需要通过以下方式来实现：\n\n**操作方案：**\n1. 删除现有的 medium 优先级报警\n2. 使用相同的参数重新创建一个 **high** 优先级的报警\n\n为了确保操作准确，我需要您提供：\n- **报警ID**（例如 `alarm_temp_zone_1_high`）\n- 当前报警的**高温限值**（high_limit）是多少？\n- 是否有**死区**（deadband）设置？\n- 是否有低温限值（low_limit）？\n\n请提供这些信息，我就可以帮您完成优先级提升。", "reasoning": "The get_threshold didn't return useful info. Let me try to see if there's a way to get alarm info. Actually, I realize I should just ask the user for the alarm ID since I don't have a way to list alarms.\n\nActually wait - maybe I should just try to work with what I know. The user mentioned \"高温报警\" (high temperature alarm) on TEMP_ZONE_1. A common convention might be \"alarm_temp_zone_1_high\" or similar.\n\nSince I don't have a tool to update priority directly, and I can't query the existing alarm's settings, I should inform the user of the situation and ask for the alarm ID.\n\nLet me be more direct and ask for the alarm ID."}], "rag": {"enabled": false, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": false, "selected_workflow": null}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 194418, "output_tokens": 1337, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 39351.085099973716}, "judge": null}
